description:
Design a 2-to-4 demultiplexer that routes a binary input signal (X) to one of four output lines (Ys) based on the value of an enable signal (En). When En is asserted (non-zero), the value of X determines which of the four outputs is activated: if X is 00, output 1 is activated; if X is 01, output 2 is activated; if X is 10, output 4 is activated; and if X is 11, output 8 is activated. If En is deasserted (zero), all outputs are driven to zero.
module top_module(

En, X, Ys

);

code:
module top_module(

En, X, Ys

);input En;
input [1:0] X;
output reg [3:0] Ys;

always @ (X, En)
begin
    if (En != 0)
    begin
            case (X)
                2'd0:
                    Ys = 4'd1;
                2'd1:
                    Ys = 4'd2;
                2'd2:
                    Ys = 4'd4;
                2'd3:
                    Ys = 4'd8;

                default:
                    Ys = 4'd0;
            endcase
    end
    else
    begin
        Ys=0;
    end
end

endmodule

