description:
Design a circuit that performs a bitwise multiplication of two 100-bit binary numbers, producing a 200-bit product. The module uses nested loops to iterate over each bit of the inputs, effectively calculating the product by simulating the elementary multiplication process. The resulting bits are accumulated in a temporary register that is subsequently assigned to the output.
module top_module(
  input [99:0] a,
  input [99:0] b,
  output [199:0] product
);

code:
module top_module(
  input [99:0] a,
  input [99:0] b,
  output [199:0] product
);reg [199:0] temp_product;
  integer i, j;

  always @(*) begin
    temp_product = 0;
    for (i = 0; i < 100; i = i + 1) begin
      for (j = 0; j < 100; j = j + 1) begin
        if (a[i] & b[j]) begin
          temp_product[i+j] = temp_product[i+j] ^ 1'b1;
        end
      end
    end
  end

  assign product = temp_product;

endmodule

