description:
Design a synchronous D flip-flop with additional control features for reset, set, toggle enable, and test input. The module accepts a clock signal (CK) and data input (D), and implements active-low reset (RN) and set (SN) functionalities. When RN is low, the output is reset to 0; when SN is low, the output is set to 1. The toggle enable (TE) dictates whether the output follows the D input when it is high. The test input (TI) provides an alternative path for the output, allowing the output to reflect the D input when TI is high, enabling testing or debugging functionalities. The module is suitable for use in sequential logic designs requiring controlled data storage with additional testing capabilities.
module top_module(
  input CK, D, RN, SN, TE, TI,
  output Q
);

code:
module top_module(
  input CK, D, RN, SN, TE, TI,
  output Q
);reg Q_reg;
  wire Q_next;

  // Implement the flip-flop with active-low reset and set
  always @(posedge CK or negedge RN or negedge SN) begin
    if (!RN) begin
      Q_reg <= 0;
    end else if (!SN) begin
      Q_reg <= 1;
    end else if (!TE) begin
      // Do nothing
    end else begin
      Q_reg <= D;
    end
  end

  // Implement the TI control signal
  assign Q_next = (TI) ? D : Q_reg;

  // Implement the output Q
  assign Q = Q_next;

endmodule

