description:
Design a multi-stage pipeline register module that allows for sequential data storage and transfer. It takes an n-bit wide input and outputs an m-bit wide signal after passing through a specified depth of pipeline stages. On each clock cycle, the input data is shifted through the pipeline, with the most recent input being stored in the first stage and existing values being shifted toward the output. This design is useful in digital circuits requiring delayed signal processing and helps in managing data flow in applications such as digital signal processing or CPU architectures.
module top_module(
  input [n-1:0] in,
  input clk,            // Added clock input
  output [m-1:0] out
);

code:
module top_module(
  input [n-1:0] in,
  input clk,            // Added clock input
  output [m-1:0] out
);parameter n = 4; // number of input signals
parameter m = 2; // number of output signals
parameter depth = 4; // depth of pipeline register

reg [n-1:0] pipeline [0:depth-1];

assign out = pipeline[depth-1];

integer i;
always @(posedge clk) begin
  for (i = depth-1; i > 0; i = i - 1) begin
    pipeline[i] <= pipeline[i-1];
  end
  pipeline[0] <= in;
end

endmodule

