description:
Design a circuit that implements an asynchronous reset functionality which drives a synchronized reset signal. When the reset input (rst) is low, the output (rst_n) is asserted low (indicating an active reset state) irrespective of the clock. On the next rising edge of the clock, if the reset input is high, the synchronized reset signal becomes high, thereby releasing the reset condition. The output rst_n is the inverted value of the synchronized reset signal, providing a clear active-low reset output.
module top_module(
  input rst,
  input clk,
  output rst_n
);

